      "title": "Qt: Workaround apparent Qt bug in delgate sizeHint with decoration",
      "message": "Qt: Workaround apparent Qt bug in delgate sizeHint with decoration\n\nQStyledItemDelegate::sizeHint requires a nonzero decoration height\n(thus, a valid decoration size) in order to properly account for the\ndecoration when returning the sizeHint. However, a nonzero decoration\nheight causes the sizeHint height to be increased by at least two\npixels, even if the decoration height plus two pixels is still less\nthan the sizeHint for the undecorated delegate. This is intentional\nby Qt, to \"prevent icons from overlapping\":\nhttps://github.com/qt/qtbase/blob/a0e0425a107aebf8727673505ea2376400b54b07/src/widgets/styles/qcommonstyle.cpp#L5027\n\nWork around this by calculating the sizeHint twice, once without and\nonce with the decoration, and taking the width from one and the height\nfrom the other. (We have to add the decoration in the size hint, because\nadding it in initStyleOption makes it get used automatically elsewhere\nand still increases the height.)\n\nFollowup to 25c29cb503cd3a7e3d7de5b70c3aa3ae8a090b7b\n",
      "author_name": "John Thacker",
      "author_email": "johnthacker@gmail.com",
      "authored_date": "2025-04-05T06:28:02.000-04:00",
